@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000

### Health: 200 Healthy with the database running, 503 Unhealthy with it stopped
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/health

### Catalog categories: 200 with the 5 seeded categories, no login needed
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/catalog/categories

### Catalog products of "Combos" (seed id): 200 with 4 products
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/catalog/products?categoryId=10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### Catalog products without categoryId: 400 problem details
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/catalog/products

### Kitchen queue: 200 with the active orders oldest first for Kitchen or Manager, 401 without a token, 403 for a Waiter
# Sign in first (POST /api/v1/auth/login/pin) and paste the accessToken in the variable below
@accessToken = paste-the-access-token-here
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/kitchen/queue
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Active orders of the signed-in waiter: 200 with the orders in New, InPreparation or Ready, 403 for kitchen or manager
# Sign in as a waiter first (POST /api/v1/auth/login/pin) and paste the accessToken in the variable of the kitchen request
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/active
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Mark an order as delivered: 200 when it is Ready, 409 when it is not Ready yet or was already delivered, 404 for another waiter's order
# Sign in as a waiter first (POST /api/v1/auth/login/pin) and use the id of one of the waiter's orders that the kitchen marked Ready
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/deliver
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Pickup orders of customers that are Ready and wait to be handed over: 200 for a waiter, 403 for kitchen or manager
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/pickups/ready
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Pickup order of a customer without login: 201 with the order number, 400 with the field errors, 409 at the third active order of a phone, 429 over the limit
# Use a new clientOrderId for every order; sending the same one again answers 200 with the order already saved
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/public/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "clientOrderId": "3f2b8c1e-5a4d-4e6f-9b7a-1c2d3e4f5a6b",
  "name": "Ana María",
  "phone": "7711234567",
  "items": [{ "productId": "20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000005", "quantity": 2 }]
}

### Follow a pickup order with the clientOrderId the phone kept: 200, or 404 when it is not a pickup order
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/public/orders/3f2b8c1e-5a4d-4e6f-9b7a-1c2d3e4f5a6b
